# ABSTRACT

The Smart Home Energy Monitoring System is an Internet of Things (IoT)-based solution developed to monitor household electricity consumption in real time. The project uses an ESP32 microcontroller, Wokwi simulation platform, and ThingSpeak cloud platform to track electrical parameters such as voltage, current, power consumption, energy usage, and estimated electricity cost.

The system helps users identify excessive power consumption and encourages energy-efficient practices. A potentiometer is used in simulation to mimic real-time current variations. Based on energy usage, LED indicators and a buzzer provide visual and audio alerts for low, moderate, and high energy consumption levels. Real-time sensor data is uploaded to ThingSpeak for remote monitoring and analysis through graphical dashboards.

This project demonstrates how IoT can improve smart home automation and energy management while reducing electricity wastage.

---

# INTRODUCTION

Energy management has become one of the most important concerns in modern households due to increasing electricity costs and excessive energy consumption. Traditional electricity meters only provide monthly readings, making it difficult for users to monitor power usage in real time.

The Smart Home Energy Monitoring System aims to solve this problem by continuously tracking electricity consumption and displaying live energy data on a cloud dashboard. By using IoT technology, the system enables users to remotely monitor their electricity usage and receive alerts during high energy consumption.

This system combines simulation, cloud computing, and embedded systems to create a cost-effective and scalable smart energy monitoring solution.

---

# PROBLEM STATEMENT

Many households face difficulties in monitoring real-time energy consumption, leading to excessive electricity usage and increased energy bills. Traditional monitoring systems do not provide instant feedback or cloud-based analytics.

Therefore, an intelligent IoT-based energy monitoring system is required to monitor energy usage, provide alerts, and display live data remotely.

---

# OBJECTIVES

The main objectives of this project are:

1. To monitor household energy consumption in real time.
2. To calculate voltage, current, power, and energy usage.
3. To estimate electricity cost automatically.
4. To provide alerts during excessive power usage.
5. To upload real-time data to ThingSpeak cloud.
6. To visualize electricity consumption through graphs and dashboards.

